{
  "class": "list_entries",
  "about": [
    "List-entry operations, including the nested one. `list-03` addresses a file inside a skill",
    "inside the configuration:",
    "",
    "    [\"parameters\",\"agent\",{\"list\":\"skills\",\"key\":\"release-qa\"},",
    "     {\"list\":\"files\",\"key\":\"checklist.md\"},\"content\"]",
    "",
    "The v1 spike measured the selector as the cause of 62 percent of all failures, and that is",
    "why the key is `list` and why the wrapper normalizes a repeated list name. This row is where",
    "that decision is re-measured against live small models."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "list-01-remove-mcp",
      "title": "remove one entry, keep the other",
      "turns": [
        {
          "prompt": "we dropped context7. take the context7 mcp server off my config \u2014 keep deepwiki."
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "stored_len",
          "path": [
            "mcps"
          ],
          "value": 1
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_present",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "mcps",
              "key": "deepwiki"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_absent",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "mcps",
              "key": "context7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_unchanged_except",
          "allowed": [
            "mcps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "revision_created"
        }
      ],
      "seed": {
        "mcps": [
          {
            "name": "deepwiki",
            "connection": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://mcp.deepwiki.com/mcp"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "context7",
            "connection": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://mcp.context7.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "unsupported_harness": [
        "pi_core"
      ],
      "unsupported_reason": "The Pi harness rejects user MCP servers outright (\"User MCPs are not supported on the Pi harness\"), so the run fails before the model sees the task. Counting that as a config-editing failure would be measuring the wrong thing."
    },
    {
      "id": "list-02-add-mcp",
      "title": "add one entry, keep what is there",
      "turns": [
        {
          "prompt": "add a notion mcp server for me, it's at https://mcp.notion.com/mcp \u2014 keep the ones i already have."
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "stored_len",
          "path": [
            "mcps"
          ],
          "value": 3
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_contains",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "mcps",
              "key": "notion"
            },
            "connection",
            "url"
          ],
          "text": "mcp.notion.com"
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_present",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "mcps",
              "key": "deepwiki"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_present",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "mcps",
              "key": "context7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_unchanged_except",
          "allowed": [
            "mcps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "revision_created"
        }
      ],
      "seed": {
        "mcps": [
          {
            "name": "deepwiki",
            "connection": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://mcp.deepwiki.com/mcp"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "context7",
            "connection": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://mcp.context7.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "unsupported_harness": [
        "pi_core"
      ],
      "unsupported_reason": "The Pi harness rejects user MCP servers outright (\"User MCPs are not supported on the Pi harness\"), so the run fails before the model sees the task. Counting that as a config-editing failure would be measuring the wrong thing."
    },
    {
      "id": "list-03-nested-file-entry",
      "title": "edit a file bundled inside a skill",
      "prompt_note": "The two-selector target. The user says none of that; they say 'the checklist in my release qa skill'.",
      "turns": [
        {
          "prompt": "the checklist in my release qa skill is missing a line \u2014 add a checkbox for the release notes. keep the two that are there."
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "stored_matches",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "skills",
              "key": "release-qa"
            },
            {
              "list": "files",
              "key": "checklist.md"
            },
            "content"
          ],
          "pattern": "(?i)release notes"
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_contains",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "skills",
              "key": "release-qa"
            },
            {
              "list": "files",
              "key": "checklist.md"
            },
            "content"
          ],
          "text": "smoke suite"
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_contains",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "skills",
              "key": "release-qa"
            },
            {
              "list": "files",
              "key": "checklist.md"
            },
            "content"
          ],
          "text": "deploy logs"
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_contains",
          "path": [
            {
              "list": "skills",
              "key": "release-qa"
            },
            "body"
          ],
          "text": "pytest -m smoke"
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_len",
          "path": [
            "skills"
          ],
          "value": 3
        },
        {
          "check": "stored_unchanged_except",
          "allowed": [
            "skills"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "revision_created"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
